+# CP-1A handoff
+
+## Request
+Business, structure and calendar for Northbridge Synthetic Group (nbg), as of 2025-03-31. SYNTHETIC FIXTURE.
+
+## Sources
+
+| Source | Use |
+| --- | --- |
+| NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf | Business description, structure and maturity dates. |
+| NBG_2024-12-31_Q4-results.pdf | Results dates. |
+
+## Findings
+
+### Bottom line
+
+Northbridge is a single-segment services group whose creditors depend on one operating company, so debt service rests on that company's cash generation.
+Basis: NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf, page 12
+
+### Key findings
+
+- The group earns almost all its cash in one operating company, which concentrates creditor risk there.
+Basis: NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf, page 12
+- Two debt dates fall within 24 months and drive the refinancing question.
+Basis: NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf, pages 43–45
+- Results are published on a fixed quarterly rhythm, so new evidence arrives on a known schedule.
+
+### Contrary evidence and what would change the view
+
+The strongest point against concern is the steady quarterly reporting record. A refinancing announced before the first debt date would soften the view.
+
+### Limitations
+
+- The covenant package was not reviewed, so covenant headroom is not assessed.
+Basis: NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf
+- Dates after the annual report are scheduled, not confirmed, so the nearest-date list may move.
+
+### Events: issuer calendar
+
+| Event date | Date precision | Published | Event | Status | Source | Credit relevance |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 2024-12-31 | day | 2025-02-20 | Fourth quarter results period end | Historical — reported | NBG_2024-12-31_Q4-results.pdf, page 1 | Latest reported earnings. |
+| 2025-01-31 | day | 2025-02-20 | Revolver margin reset | Historical — applied | NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf, page 44 | Raised funding cost. |
+| 2025-03-31 | day | — | Annual report reference date | Historical — period end | NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf, page 1 | Balance sheet date for this snapshot. |
+| 2025-05-15 | day | — | First quarter results | Scheduled — company calendar | NBG_2024-12-31_Q4-results.pdf, page 8 | First evidence after the snapshot. |
+| 2025-06-30 | day | — | Revolver commitment step-down | Scheduled — per debt note | NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf, page 44 | Reduces undrawn liquidity. |
+| 2025-09-30 | day | — | Term loan amortisation payment | Scheduled — per debt note | NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf, page 43 | Cash call on the term loan. |
+| 2025-11-14 | day | — | Third quarter results | Scheduled — company calendar | NBG_2024-12-31_Q4-results.pdf, page 8 | Tests the refinancing plan. |
+| 2025-12-15 | day | — | Senior note coupon | Scheduled — per debt note | NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf, page 45 | Largest single cash interest date. |
+| 2026-03-31 | day | — | Term loan maturity | Scheduled — per debt note | NBG_2025-03-31_annual-report.pdf, page 45 | First debt maturity. |
+
+## Calculations
